# pdf2htmlEX's template for its output, passed to it with --data-dir.
#
# The stock template wraps the pages in a full-window document viewer: an
# outline sidebar, a page container that is an absolutely positioned scroller
# filling the viewport, a loading indicator and the script that drives them.
# All of that assumes the document owns the browser window, which no PDF
# converted here ever does: it becomes a document set member, shown in a
# viewer's frame, or is merged into the back of the report, where a viewport
# scroller draws over the top of the report. So this template is the page
# content alone, styled by base.css.
#
# Syntax, as for the stock manifest: lines starting with # are comments; text
# between lines of """ is copied verbatim; @file embeds a file from this
# directory; $css and $pages are the converted document's own CSS and pages.
"""
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8"/>
<meta name="generator" content="pdf2htmlEX"/>
"""
@base.css
$css
"""
<title></title>
</head>
<body>
"""
$pages
"""
</body>
</html>
"""
